  "review": "Re-read OBS-CWS-005/006/008/009/010/015 against current Notion/Airtable passages: access levels, page-level rules, attributed history, restore and automation run/configuration history remain supported. New notes preserve counterevidence: broadest permission wins in Notion; restoring a database does not restore nested page bodies; Airtable record revision history has no product export or history-read API. These do not establish the stronger Composed recovery, access and portability guarantees. REQ-CWS-030/031/032, INV-CWS-004/015 and POL-CWS-007 remain unchanged.",
  "followup": "Deepen effective permission composition, database/page/attachment restore scope, portable history and retention versus erasure; run conflict/offline and recovery fixtures. Do not transfer vendor UI guarantees to the complete workspace.",
  "behavioural_diff_from_historical_bodies": "unknown; old bodies unavailable, original metadata preserved",
